    "summary": "Cosmic Dark Star → Saint Stephen and a thunderous Eleven",
    "blurb": "The show shines with an iconic Dark Star‑Saint Stephen stretch and a searing turn on Your Lovelight. Phil’s bass thunders through The Eleven while Tom’s organ adds stellar texture. Overall the performance is tight, adventurous, and captured in crystal‑clear soundboard mixes.",
    "review": "February 27, 1969 at the Fillmore West delivered one of the early Dead’s most legendary outings. From the opening “Good Morning Little School Girl” through a blistering first set, the band already displayed tight interplay, but it was the second set that truly lifted off – a seamless segue from “Mountains Of The Moon” into an otherworldly Dark Star that morphs into a soaring Saint Stephen, followed by Phil’s thunderous bass on the manic “The Eleven”. The night closed with a blazing “Turn On Your Lovelight”, showcasing Jerry’s fiery solo work, while Tom Constanten’s organ weaves through the extended Cryptical Envelopment → The Other One suite. The encore “Cosmic Charlie” caps off a performance that feels both historic and freshly exhilarating, all preserved in an excellent 16‑track soundboard capture that balances the band’s dynamics with remarkable clarity.",
